    "text": "The lamps go thin, the console size, and all this shade. Behind my eyes. There are mornings with no handle, only carpet wall and weight. Every thought a lock is set, every limeloting gate. Then I find the hidden rail from the drawer beside the bed. Small, bright, current, plain provision for the system in the red. No romance in the rescue, no cathedral, no parade. Just a backup voltage humming, where the human battery free. Back up rail, hold the body, when the main line disappears. Bring the color to the panel, bring the floorboards back from Smith. Don't worship the small lighting, I just need the room to stay. When the screen begins to turn, you return me to the day. People call it little comfort, as if comfort were a flaw. As if every fragile engine, not a run-on line. But I know the sound of empty, when the meat is barely left. I know how the whole apartment tilts around, the missing gift. So I keep a measured signal, not for pleasure, not for grace. Just a key, the old receiver from dissolving out of place. Dependences and ugly words, until the rail goes cold. And every theory loses voltage, and the body tells the truth. Back up rail, hold the body, when the main line disappears. Bring the color to the panel, bring the floorboards back from Smith. Don't worship the small lighting, I just need the room to stay. When the screen begins to turn, you return me to the day. When the screen starts to turn, you return me to the day. Just the current With my name",
